    "SASH WINDOWS (COMPLIANCE): All new sash windows shall be painted timber double-hung sash windows with a slim profile. Where glazing bars are shown on the approved drawings these shall be narrow integral (not applied) glazing bars with a putty finish (not timber bead). The glazing shall be no greater than 14mm in total thickness. No visible trickle vents or metallic/perforated spacer bars are permitted. \r\n\r\nREASON: To preserve the character and appearance of the conservation area."
